Here's the modernized version using type-safe ValueTuples (MSTest 3.7+):

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DynamicData(nameof(TestData))]
public void Validate_ReturnsExpected(string input, bool expected)
{
    var result = Validator.IsValid(input);
    Assert.AreEqual(expected, result);
}

public static IEnumerable<(string input, bool expected)> TestData =>
[
    ("valid@email.com", true),
    ("invalid", false),
    ("", false),
];
```

**Key changes:**
- `IEnumerable<object[]>` → `IEnumerable<(string input, bool expected)>` for compile-time type safety
- `["value", true]` (object arrays) → `("value", true)` (ValueTuples)
- Named tuple elements serve as self-documentation
- Test method signature stays the same — MSTest auto-deconstructs the tuple into parameters
